extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 6: South America, printed 117-118 (cache p118-p119), read from the text layer. ONE STAT BLOCK FOR TWO CREATURES: the heading is Werejaguars & Werepanthers, the stats are the werejaguar''s, and the werepanther is named only as its cousin with no numbers of its own. Stored as two variants that carry nothing but a name. S.D.C./M.D.C.: the entry prints Hit Points (Special) 6D6+10 and no S.D.C. or M.D.C. formula; men_of_arms false, the race rule. HIT POINTS: the skills paragraph says hit points increase with each level but prints no per-level die; only 6d6+10 is stored. EXPERIENCE: printed ''same as psi-stalker'' twice (the Experience Level line and the Skills line). psi-stalker in production stores no xp_table, so none is stored here. Average NPC level 1D4 is not stored. ONE SHAPE IS MODELLED, the Man-Wolf precedent: the class''s own block is the natural half-beast shape (attacks_base 5, horror_factor 12). The human shape (two attacks per melee, no Horror Factor) and the animal shape (the same five attacks) are prose. second_form was considered and not used: its toggle tracks damage separately per form, and this creature has ONE body and one Hit Point pool across its shapes, so switching would read as healing. ATTRIBUTES: P.S. and P.P. are 4D6, never less than 16, stored as attribute_minimums. BONUSES: +1 initiative, +2 strike, +2 parry and dodge, +6 save vs Horror Factor, +2 save vs psionics, +2 save vs magic - stored as spell_magic only; the book does not say magic of any kind. MAGIC: seven spells cast from its own P.P.E., granted by name, no picks. PSIONICS: three powers and I.S.P. 5D6; no tier is printed and none is written. SKILLS: Spanish 98% and land navigation 90% are fixed. Prowl 80, swim 60, climb 90/80 and acrobatics 80 are printed as natural abilities and granted as catalog skills at a fixed figure (the Man-Wolf precedent); track by smell 60% stays a natural ability, as no catalog row is scent tracking. The book calls the rest secondary skills: seven at level one and two more at 3, 6, 9, 11 and 14, stored as secondary_skills with the printed categories (the Gargoyle and Wild Vampire precedent for an R.C.C. played without an occupation). Technical ''language'' is Language: Other; ''lore'' is every Technical-category Lore row in the catalog; ''boat'' is the three small-boat rows (Ships and Submersibles left out - a judgement); ''horsemanship'' is Horsemanship: General. The Wilderness +20% cannot ride a secondary pick and is in the note. No hand to hand is printed and none is granted."
