# Werejaguar / Werepanther

## Lore

The Jaguar People are shape-changers of Central and South America, most
numerous around Omagua and the Yucatan. Outside the city they live in small
tribes and villages of a few dozen to about a hundred. They worship
Yaguar-Ogui, the jaguar god, who sometimes calls on them in times of need; in
ancient times they called themselves his Children. Their werepanther cousins
share the same nature.

Thousands moved to Omagua when it was founded, and most of the werebeasts there
serve in its armed forces, which gives them a reason to go hunting animals and
supernatural monsters in the jungle. They get along with the other feline races,
though a rivalry with the hunter cats sometimes turns ugly.

Myth calls them the enemy of man, but they usually avoid humans unless defending
themselves or their land. They prey on animals and supernatural creatures, and
are instinctive enemies of vampires. They love a hunt for sport - the stalking
and the chase more than the kill - and a captive who is not a vampire or a demon
is often let go once the game is over.

## GM Notes

The book gives one stat block for both creatures. A werepanther is the
werejaguar with a panther''s shape.
